          "summary": "Convert mutual no-hire into a narrow 12-month mutual non-solicit limited to personnel involved in the services, with general-advertising and unsolicited-approach carve-outs",
          "comment": "[Playbook] We cannot accept a no-hire covering all of the other party's employees, so we have replaced it with a mutual non-solicitation limited to individuals directly involved in the services, running 12 months from the end of their involvement, with the customary carve-outs for general advertising and unsolicited approaches. Our preferred position is no such restriction on us at all, but we are content with this narrowed mutual formulation.",
          "ops": [
            {
              "kind": "replace",
              "paragraphId": "p0133",
              "oldText": "During the term of this Agreement and for a period of one year thereafter, both parties agree not to hire or allow its respective affiliates to hire any employee of the other party, or any person who was an employee of the other party during the previous six months and who was directly involved in the provision of services under this Agreement.",
              "newText": "During the term of this Agreement and for a period of twelve (12) months after the end of an individual's involvement in the provision of services under this Agreement, neither party will, and neither party will permit its affiliates to, directly solicit for employment any employee of the other party who was directly involved in the provision of services under this Agreement. This Section does not prohibit either party from hiring any person, and does not apply to general advertisements or other recruitment efforts not specifically targeted at the other party's personnel, or to any person who approaches a party on an unsolicited basis or who responds to such general recruitment."
